# NTL master pool

Every public Name That LLM passage set we know of, merged into one parquet file (`ntl_public_pool_v2.parquet`: `text`, `model`, `group`, `src`, `w`) and cleaned the same way.

**Base:** crtproduction's open pool (`crtproduction/name-that-llm-open-pool`, its author-cleaned release) and Dhruv Tibarewal's matched pool (`dhruvtibarewal/nlm-matched-clean`), plus the other public passage datasets of the competition (see the `src` column).

**Cleaning applied to every source:**
- rows the open pool's author removed are dropped wherever else the same text appears;
- refusals, chat preambles, API dumps, CJK text, cut-off text, multi-paragraph or markdown text, and passages outside 36-275 words are dropped;
- typography a model never uses in the official train set, near-copies of train passages and passages on a train prompt's topic are dropped, as are exact duplicates;
- gemini-3.7-flash rows are kept only where 3.7 was really served;
- a label audit (after samarth1006's idea): kimi-k3 rows from sources whose kimi-k3 passages a model trained only on the official data almost never recognises are dropped.

About 234k passages over the 18 competition labels. Credits: crtproduction, Dhruv Tibarewal, samarth1006 and every author of the public passage sets merged here.
